    "electric_vehicle": {
      "path": "electric_vehicle",
      "structuralHash": "2baa3d696c348682d0f1bae47cc49edba66877eb34e553c3e36d151bfefcad83",
      "description": "The electric_vehicle subsystem integrates multiple components to simulate the behavior of an electric vehicle. It includes a core vehicle model, electrical system dynamics, and state-of-charge (SOC) estimation.\n\nKey components:\n- Vehicle: Models the primary physical dynamics such as motion, forces, and interactions with the environment.\n- Electrical_system: Manages power sources, sensors, actuators, and motor control via H-Bridge and PWM signals. Interfaces with mechanical components through rotational references using PMIOPorts.\n- SOC: Calculates the State of Charge of the battery based on input current and internal parameters using a discrete-time integrator and rate transition blocks to ensure sampling consistency.\n\nThe subsystem connects these elements into a cohesive simulation environment where vehicle dynamics are influenced by electrical power management. It supports real-time simulations for evaluating performance under various drive cycles, with outputs such as velocity and distance monitored through scopes. This setup enables comprehensive analysis of electric vehicle behavior from both mechanical and electrical perspectives.",
